lice, Yin, Xuwang, Trevino, Eduardo, Geralnik, Matias, Khoja, Adam, Lee, Dean, Yue, Summer, Hendrycks, Dan. Metadata date: ['2025/03/05']; 22 pages. [Source](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.03750).\n- [Liars&#39; Bench: Evaluating Lie Detectors for Language Models](2511.16035.pdf) — Kretschmar, Kieron, Laurito, Walter, Maiya, Sharan, Marks, Samuel. Metadata date: ['2025/11/20']; 112 pages. [Source](https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.16035).\n- [Detecting Strategic Deception Using Linear Probes](2502.03407.pdf) — Goldowsky-Dill, Nicholas, Chughtai, Bilal, Heimersheim, Stefan, Hobbhahn, Marius. Metadata date: ['2025/02/05']; 35 pages. [Source](https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.03407).\n- [One Probe Won&#39;t Catch Them All: Towards Targeted Deception Detection](2602.01425.pdf) — Natarajan, Vikram, Jain, Devina, Arora, Shivam, Golechha, Satvik, Bloom, Joseph. Metadata date: ['2026/02/01']; 16 pages. [Source](https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.01425).\n- [Probing the Limits of the Lie Detector Approach to LLM Deception](2603.10003.pdf) — Thormann, Tom-Felix. Metadata date: ['2026/02/16']; 10 pages. [Source](https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.10003).\n- [Asymmetries in Spontaneous and Instructed Deception](2609.00180.pdf) — Luikham, Josiah. Metadata date: ['2026/08/31']; 22 pages. [Source](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.00180).\n- [Beyond Liars&#39; Bench: The Impact of Lie Typology, Depth, and Sparsity on Deception Detection in LLMs](2607.20479.pdf) — Moustafa, Amr, Feser, Max, Mai, Florian. Metadata date: ['2026/05/29']; 9 pages. [Source](https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.20479).\n- [Do LLMs Really Know What They Don&#39;t Know? Internal States Mainly Reflect Knowledge Recall Rather Than Truthfulness](2510.09033.pdf) — Cheang, Chi Seng, Chan, Hou Pong, Zhang, Wenxuan, Deng, Yang. Metadata date: ['2025/10/10']; 18 pages. [Source](https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.09033).\n- [&#34;Did you lie?&#34; Evaluating Lie Detectors across Model Scale and Belief-Verified Model Organisms](2606.12618.pdf) — Cooney, Alan, Africa, David, Irving, Geoffrey. Metadata date: ['2026/06/10']; 32 pages. [Source](https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.12618).\n- [Semantic Entropy Probes: Robust and Cheap Hallucination Detection in LLMs](2406.15927.pdf) — Kossen, Jannik, Han, Jiatong, Razzak, Muhammed, Schut, Lisa, Malik, Shreshth, Gal, Yarin. Metadata date: ['2024/06/22']; 22 pages. [Source](https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.15927).\n\nThe specified [Anthropic article](https://alignment.anthropic.com/2026/lie-detectors/) is an HTML publication, saved in `notes/anthropic_lie_detectors.html`, not counted as a PDF. Chunk PDFs/manifests are in `pages/`; reproducible chunker command: `.venv/bin/python .codex/skills/paper-finder/scripts/pdf_chunker.py papers/ID.pdf --pages-per-chunk 6`.\n/usr/bin/pdflatex\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
